xnu 0228: give CP_EVENT_WRITE the BIT(27) this CP requires

The GL self test in the CoreAnimation shim settles what kept the panel black: a
framebuffer-complete texture cleared to red reads back as zeros, so nothing the
Adreno renders reaches memory. freedreno drives the RB blit engine with
CP_EVENT_WRITE -- FD_BLIT (event 30) is what makes a clear happen and what
resolves a tile out of GMEM into the render target (a6xx/fd6_emit.h,
fd6_emit_blit()), FD_CACHE_CLEAN (0x31) pushes the GPU's own writes out of its
cache -- and this CP refuses an event write without BIT(27) in its event dword
(CP_INTERRUPT_STATUS bit 7, CP_ILLEGAL_INSTR_ERROR). That refusal is the same
one that made this port's ring fence a CP_MEM_WRITE (0181, cpfence=mem), and
the form that was measured working there is CACHE_CLEAN|BIT(27).

The user client rewrites every CP_EVENT_WRITE in a submission, and in the
indirect buffers it chains, to that form: one OR of BIT(27) into the event
dword, then a write-back of the buffer, because the CP fetches from memory and
the changed dwords are in the CPU's cache. gpuevent=0 leaves the streams alone
for the A/B.
